{"title":"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/3/e53b1fe25be1c679117fb44a6a886fe1247d189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> of real numbers which satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/1/b218cbec3b08792c719300e9d099d5c90b4d7f82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3-y^3=4(x-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/c/c3ca880e7a6271c9f6fe207aa5952fef2dafb51e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3+y^3=2(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"145\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Factoring and rearranging terms for both equations results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f5c3444200a98ec88589f52de8fd288480175f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-y)(x^2 + xy + y^2 - 4) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f16109d4522e3fb6e7cbb9c187ef336f53a2d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)(x^2 - xy + y^2 - 2) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"19\" />.  By the Zero Product Property, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/3/2e33fa7c7b2ce1a18e6e0a6d3ef6c08bd1958722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fb82667bd96eaac36929055d82b92803861b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + xy + y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> in the first equation, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/f/ebfdcae3053a174486c115cae26db3ee6a837c6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/baec7d38db576faedfe325e6e63f7e90a6a2aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy + y^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> in the second equation.  In order for the solution to satisfy both equations, it must satisfy at least one of the conditions in each equation.  Now there are four cases to consider.\n</p><p><b>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c6f440a0a502b9742ddfe66649ed66b834d8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"11\" /></b>\n</p><p>Solving this system results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f9603ca3089464e548fc6f1366bc474e7efef8d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"20\" />.  Plugging the x and y values back in satisfies the original equation.\n</p><p><b>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/baec7d38db576faedfe325e6e63f7e90a6a2aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy + y^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /></b>\n</p><p>Substitution results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/8007eb760d5640c38d7ee3d90b27fe6f56ca9cc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = 2$\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />, so solving this system results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268f6203d803dc7fc4bd1a7e75493a8e48eb9817.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0b698c107bce203f3674858acfcfb5c3c63478.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />.  Plugging the x and y values back in for each ordered pair satisfies the original equation.\n</p><p><b>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fb82667bd96eaac36929055d82b92803861b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + xy + y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52c6f440a0a502b9742ddfe66649ed66b834d8ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"57\" height=\"11\" /></b>\n</p><p>Substitution results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/f/4cfe9dee9218afdb2f79456b507c5a323484f3ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />, so solving this system results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/211f55c01222ffbccc389f0d79159ad07ad77d48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a95882ef79b538a727f5eb550c3a9810a7b28674.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />.  Plugging the x and y values back in for each ordered pair satisfies the original equation.\n</p><p><b>Case 4: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/f/c0fb82667bd96eaac36929055d82b92803861b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + xy + y^2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/baec7d38db576faedfe325e6e63f7e90a6a2aca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - xy + y^2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /></b>\n</p><p>Subtracting the second equation from the first equation results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03df4bb7509203a5e96760a0bedbbe3f668da90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2xy = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598dc22afe2486653a8ef80602915f2b457815f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/0/010b97503c0bc314883d30558a75154ed1a456c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + y^2 = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/0/330f5340522c6f1e9573fc78597ea77e34a170ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\tfrac{1}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/5/1d5d630dc8df3c8d19af10daa067ab2ad3694374.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + \\tfrac{1}{x^2} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"91\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nMultiplying both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and bringing all terms to one side results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3f840a1f240a15a05df5136feabfc1f34595432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 - 3x^2 + 1 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />.  By using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Quadratic_Formula\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Quadratic Formula\">Quadratic Formula</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/c/0bc9776d89878c9f4d74615f9b2f6344c3270930.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = \\tfrac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"79\" height=\"24\" />, and both quantities are positive.  If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd82d4276716a44f919f762a9b7f3f68924ef0fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 = \\tfrac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"79\" height=\"24\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/986a555b2441991aea819e0ef78efcf53d84e76d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^2 = \\tfrac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"78\" height=\"24\" /> (and vice versa).  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/8/598dc22afe2486653a8ef80602915f2b457815f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> must have the same sign.\n</p><p><br />\nTherefore, there are four ordered pairs — <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/2/b82c1becfb71f684ab0a7947b9cd28e56ebb1ae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}},\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}), (-\\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}, -\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"394\" height=\"53\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/7/3671d8812faebb5fc0c000dc3021e8f2a43b6b90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}, \\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}), (-\\sqrt{\\frac{3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2}}, -\\sqrt{\\frac{3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2}}).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"393\" height=\"53\" />  Plugging the x and y values back in for each ordered pair satisfies the original equation.\n</p><p><br />\nIn total, there are nine ordered pairs of real numbers that satisfy the original equation, which are listed in each case.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO\">2006 Indonesia MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Indonesia_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Indonesia MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Indonesia_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Indonesia MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017131043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 231/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1007/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 59/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7325/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.322      1 Template:Indonesia_MO_box\n100.00%   10.322      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17767:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017131043 and revision id 119624. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}